lt={"A savings jar, a set of new keys and a floor plan on an oak table"} width={"2000"} height={"1125"} fetchPriority={"high"} decoding={"async"} style={{"objectPosition": "50% 55%"}} /></figure></div></section><section id={"mg-ar-body"} className={"custom-section"} aria-label={"The guide"}><div className={"container grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 xl:grid-cols-[14rem_minmax(0,1fr)] xl:gap-x-[clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem)]"}><aside className={"custom-ar-meta grid [align-content:start] xl:sticky xl:top-8 xl:[align-self:start]"} aria-label={"About this guide"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><p className={"flex items-center gap-3 mt-0"}><img className={"size-11 rounded-full object-cover object-[50%_20%]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/800x1067.svg"} alt={""} width={"800"} height={"1067"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><span className={"grid text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.35] text-soft"}><strong className={"text-[1rem] font-semibold text-text"}>{"Charlotte Hale"}</strong>{"CeMAP adviser"}</span></p><dl className={"custom-ar-facts grid"}><div><dt className={"text-[0.9375rem] text-soft"}>{"Published"}</dt><dd className={"mt-0.5 font-semibold"}><time datetime={"2026-08-12"}>{"12 August 2026"}</time></dd></div><div><dt className={"text-[0.9375rem] text-soft"}>{"Topic"}</dt><dd className={"mt-0.5 font-semibold"}>{"First-Time Buyers"}</dd></div><div><dt className={"text-[0.9375rem] text-soft"}>{"Reading Time"}</dt><dd className={"mt-0.5 font-semibold"}>{"6 min"}</dd></div></dl><div className={"social-share"}><span className={"social-share-label"}>{"Share"}</span><ul className={"social-list"} role={"list"}><li><button type={"button"} className={"btn btn-circle btn-copy"} data-copy-url={""} data-copy-done={"Link copied"} aria-label={"Copy the link to this guide"}><i className={"ph ph-link"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><span className={"sr-only"} data-copy-label={""} aria-live={"polite"}></span></button></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} aria-label={"Share on Facebook"}><i className={"ph ph-facebook-logo"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li><li><a href={"mailto:?subject=How%20much%20deposit%20do%20you%20really%20need%3F"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} aria-label={"Share by email"}><i className={"ph ph-envelope-simple"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li></ul></div></aside><article className={"custom-ar-body max-w-[68ch] text-[1.125rem] leading-[1.75] text-text"}><p className={"font-heading text-[clamp(1.25rem,1.15rem_+_0.4vw,1.4375rem)] font-medium leading-[1.6]"}>{"It’s the first question almost everyone asks us, and the honest answer is: less than you think, but more than the minimum is usually worth it. A deposit does two jobs. It gets a lender to say yes, and it decides which rates you’re offered once they do."}</p><p>{"Most lenders will lend up to 95% of a home’s price, so the smallest deposit is 5%. On a £250,000 flat that’s £12,500. Plenty of our first-time buyers start there, and it’s a perfectly sensible place to be."}</p><h2>{"Why the steps matter"}</h2><p className={"mt-4"}>{"Lenders price their deals in bands of loan to value, or LTV. Cross from one band into the next and the rate drops, sometimes sharply. The biggest jumps tend to come at 90%, 85% and 75%."}</p><figure className={"custom-ar-table mt-9 p-[clamp(1.25rem,1rem_+_1vw,1.75rem)] rounded-(--custom-radius-card) bg-(--custom-card)"}><figcaption className={"font-heading font-bold leading-[1.4]"}>{"A £250,000 home over 25 years, on a 5-year fix"}</figcaption><table className={"w-full mt-3 text-[1rem] leading-[1.4] lining-nums tabular-nums"}><thead><tr><th className={"text-left text-[0.9375rem] font-medium text-soft"} scope={"col"}>{"Deposit"}</th><th className={"text-left text-[0.9375rem] font-medium text-soft"} scope={"col"}>{"Loan to value"}</th><th className={"text-left text-[0.9375rem] font-medium text-soft"} scope={"col"}>{"Typical rate"}</th><th className={"text-right text-[0.9375rem] font-medium text-soft"} scope={"col"}>{"Monthly"}</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className={"border-t border-t-(--color-border)"}><th className={"text-left font-bold"} scope={"row"}>{"£12,500"}</th><td className={"text-left"}>{"95%"}</td><td className={"text-left"}>{"4.75%"}</td><td className={"text-right font-heading font-bold"}>{"£1,354"}</td></tr><tr className={"border-t border-t-(--color-border)"}><th className={"text-left font-bold"} scope={"row"}>{"£25,000"}</th><td className={"text-left"}>{"90%"}</td><td className={"text-left"}>{"4.45%"}</td><td className={"text-right font-heading font-bold"}>{"£1,244"}</td></tr><tr className={"border-t border-t-(--color-border)"}><th className={"text-left font-bold"} scope={"row"}>{"£37,500"}</th><td className={"text-left"}>{"85%"}</td><td className={"text-left"}>{"4.23%"}</td><td className={"text-right font-heading font-bold"}>{"£1,149"}</td></tr><tr className={"border-t border-t-(--color-border)"}><th className={"text-left font-bold"} scope={"row"}>{"£62,500"}</th><td className={"text-left"}>{"75%"}</td><td className={"text-left"}>{"4.01%"}</td><td className={"text-right font-heading font-bold"}>{"£991"}</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p className={"custom-small mt-3"}>{"Illustrative rates, as at 30 June 2026. "}<strong>{"Your home may be repossessed if you do not keep up repayments on your mortgage."}</strong></p><p>{"Going from 5% to 10% saves about £110 a month in this example, or more than £6,500 over a five-year fix. That’s the moment many buyers decide a few more months of saving is worth it."}</p><blockquote className={"custom-ar-quote mt-12 mb-12"}><p className={"font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.25rem_+_1vw,2rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance"}>{"The best deposit isn’t the biggest one. It’s the one that gets you over the next rate band."}</p></blockquote><h2>{"When to stop saving"}</h2><p className={"mt-4"}>{"Waiting has a cost too: another year of rent, and prices that may move while you save. If you’re just short of a band, it’s usually worth closing the gap. If the next band is a year away, buying now and remortgaging later can come out ahead."}</p><p>{"A gifted deposit from family counts exactly like your own savings, as long as it’s a gift and not a loan. A Lifetime ISA adds a quarter on top of what you put in, up to £1,000 a year."}</p><h2>{"Don’t forget the extras"}</h2><p className={"mt-4"}>{"Keep £2,500 to £4,000 aside for the solicitor, searches, a survey and the move itself. First-time buyers pay no stamp duty up to £300,000, which helps more than people expect."}</p><p>{"If you’d like us to run your own numbers, a twenty-minute call is usually enough. We’ll tell you which band you’re in, how close the next one is and whether it’s worth the wait."}</p><p className={"font-semibold text-soft"}>{"— Charlotte Hale, Manchester"}</p></article></div></section><section id={"mg-ar-related"} className={"custom-section"} aria-labelledby={"mg-ar-related-title"}><div className={"container"}><div className={"custom-head custom-head--row"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><h2 id={"mg-ar-related-title"} className={"custom-title"}>{"Read next."}</h2><a href={"#page=demo-mortgage-1-guides"} className={"btn btn-link btn-link-dark btn-link-arrow"}><span className={"link-arrow text-(--custom-accent)"} aria-hidden={"true"}></span>{"All Guides"}</a></div><ul className={"custom-guides-grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"} role={"list"}><li className={"custom-guide relative"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><div className={"custom-guide-media overflow-clip aspect-[4/3] rounded-(--custom-radius-photo) bg-soft"}><img className={"size-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1200x900.svg"} alt={"Hands holding a phone showing an approval tick beside a mug of tea"} width={"1200"} height={"900"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></div><p className={"custom-guide-meta"}><span>{"First-Time Buyers"}</span>{"3 min read"}</p><h3 className={"